From 17f1e95e661b24c4f5218fca7c0a6b21b6b45afd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "William Mark Katzenmeyer, P.E., C.F.M." <heccommander@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:10:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] hdf5-reader: keep exact datatype envelopes and expose
 raw attribute messages

[L03+L04 (vendor patches 03, 04)] Status vs upstream v0.9.3: NOT UPSTREAM.
Kind: API addition + parser hardening. Proposed upstream grouping: PR-D API proposal (breaking struct fields; discuss first).
Applies on roteiro-gis/netcdf-rust v0.9.3 (3d708fd) after the earlier patches of this series.

Add DatatypeMessage::raw_encoding and AttributeMessage::raw_datatype (the
exact encoded datatype bytes before semantic normalisation), the
non-eager Group::raw_attributes and Dataset::raw_attributes accessors,
Dataset::raw_datatype, and Error::UnsupportedEncoding. Attribute message
parsing is bounded to the declared message size, reserved attribute flags
are rejected, and shared attribute encodings report UnsupportedEncoding.

The new struct fields are a breaking change for struct-literal
constructors.
